statement:
Let m ∈ ℕ, n := m + 1, and T ∈ D_n(ℝ^n) (a GeometricCurrentOn univ n). Let v : ℝ^n → ℝ satisfy:
- v is measurable and Lebesgue integrable;
- v(x) ∈ ℤ for every x;
- whenever v(x) ≠ 0, v(y) = v(x) for all y in a neighbourhood of x.
If T(ω) = ∫ v(x) ω(x)(e_0, …, e_m) dx for every ω ∈ D^n(ℝ^n), where e_i = EuclideanSpace.single i 1, then T is integer multiplicity.
